-- title:
--   Places of X₀(N) accumulating at the cusp ∞
-- statement:
--   Fix a non-zero natural number $N$ and write $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` be the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(q)\!)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, the subfield of $\mathbb Q(\!(q)\!)$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the divisor expansions attached to $N$. A place of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is, in this development, a valuation subring of $F$ containing $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, distinct from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring; for $f$ in such a subring, `evalAt` returns the element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ mapping to the residue of $f$ in the residue field (and $0$ for $f$ outside the subring). Let $\sigma : \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathbb C$ be a ring homomorphism, $S$ a finite set of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $Y$ a finite set of elements of $F$, all assumed to lie in the valuation subring of the $q$-adic place `cuspInftyBar N` (the place built from $j$, of $q$-order $-1$). Then there is a sequence $(v_n)_{n \in \mathbb N}$ of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $v_n \notin S$ and $v_n \neq$ `cuspInftyBar N` for all $n$, such that each $y \in Y$ lies in the valuation subring of every $v_n$, satisfies $y(v_n) \neq 0$ for all $n$ whenever $y \neq 0$, and $\sigma(y(v_n)) \to \sigma(y(\text{cusp}))$ in $\mathbb C$ as $n \to \infty$, where $y(v)$ denotes `evalAt`.
--
--   This is the density statement that algebraic points of $X_0(N)$ accumulate at the cusp $\infty$ in the complex topology induced by $\sigma$, with the approximating places avoiding a prescribed finite set and keeping finitely many prescribed functions regular and non-vanishing. It is used in the construction of sequences of places converging to the cusp or to a given place, and to deduce that $X_0(N)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ has infinitely many places.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_seq_place_tendsto_evalAt_cuspInftyBar.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_AtkinLehner
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_PlaceEvaluation

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open AlgebraicCurve ModularCurve

theorem ModularCurve.exists_seq_place_tendsto_evalAt_cuspInftyBar (N : ℕ) [NeZero N]
    (σ : AlgebraicClosure ℚ →+* ℂ)
    (S : Finset (Place (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar N)))
    (Y : Finset ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar N))
    (hY : ∀ y ∈ Y, y ∈ (cuspInftyBar N).toValuationSubring) :
    ∃ v : ℕ → Place (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar N),
      (∀ n, v n ∉ S) ∧ (∀ n, v n ≠ cuspInftyBar N) ∧
      ∀ y ∈ Y, (∀ n, y ∈ (v n).toValuationSubring) ∧ (y ≠ 0 → ∀ n, (v n).evalAt y ≠ 0) ∧
        Filter.Tendsto (fun n => σ ((v n).evalAt y)) Filter.atTop
          (nhds (σ ((cuspInftyBar N).evalAt y))) := by sorry
